# Connect Domain Sheet

::summary
The custom-domain sheet (F-1 RULED 08-04), opened from the app detail's Web section: domain input (Connect disabled until text), the CNAME record to add at the registrar, then Connect runs the in-sheet probe progression — Verifying DNS → DNS verified — binding → connected, certificate issuing (prod connect+bind parity).
::

::modal[name=connect-domain title="Connect domain" width=340 placement=centered dismissible=true]

:::form[name=connect-domain submit="Connect" action=connectDomain]
- Domain (text, "e.g. gallery.example.com") *
:::

:::row[icon=doc state=readonly href=#]
Record — CNAME → tidepool.surf.space
Add at the registrar; target = the app's current public host
:::

:::row[icon=sparkle state=progress href=#]
Verifying DNS → DNS verified — binding → connected
Status line progresses in-sheet; certificate issues after bind
:::

::

Top-right ✕ per dismiss canon. Connect stays disabled until the domain field has text; the form couples the field and the Connect submit at the top, with the record and status rows beneath (reviewed order keeps Connect last — button placement is renderer polish). A failed verification keeps the sheet open with the probe error on the status line; nothing binds until DNS verifies.

At small width (≤ 767px, R-C ruling 08-10) the sheet goes edge-to-edge with 10px side insets and auto width; the wide placement declared on the block is unchanged.
